    "text": "In usses Dryhtnes naman H\u00e6lendes Cristes ic Werfer\u00f0 bisceop cy\u00f0e, swa me Alchun bisceop s\u00e6gde &\nOnd he \u00fea Eastmund \u00e6r his ende bebead on \u00fe\u00e6s lifgendan Godes noman \u00feam men \u00fee to \u00feam lande\n\u00dea \u00e6fter Eastmundes for\u00f0si\u00f0e bereafode seo m\u00e6g\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6s ilcan londes ge \u00fea gastas \u00feara for\u00f0gewitenra\n& Heaberht bisceop oft \u00fe\u00e6s myngode o\u00f0\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6s landes b\u00e6d, & seo\u00f0\u00f0an Alchun bisceop foroft \u00fea hwile\n& we ne mihton to nanum rihte becuman \u00e6r \u00e6\u00f0elred w\u00e6s Myrcna hlaford.\n\u00dea gesamnode he Mercna weotan to Saltwic ymbe m\u00e6nigfealde \u00feearfe ge Godes d\u00e6les ge worolde\n\u00dea beweddode me Eadno\u00f0 me & \u00e6lfred & \u00e6lfstan \u00fe\u00e6t hio o\u00f0er \u00feara dydon, o\u00f0\u00f0e hit me ageafon o\u00f0\u00f0e\n\u00dea Eadno\u00f0, \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t land h\u00e6fde, gebead hit ealre \u00fe\u00e6re m\u00e6g\u00f0e, hw\u00e6\u00f0er hit \u00e6nig swa gegan wolde, \u00fea\n\u00dea gesohte he \u00e6\u00f0elred & \u00e6\u00f0elfl\u00e6de & eac \u00e6\u00f0elno\u00f0 urne ealra freond.\n& heo ealle to me wilnodon \u00fe\u00e6t ic hine l\u00e6te \u00e6t me \u00fe\u00e6t land begeotan him to agenre \u00e6hte, swelcum\n& ic \u00fea swa dyde, ealles swy\u00f0ost for hiora bene.\n& he eac me gesealde feowertig mancesa.\n& ic \u00fea mid mira higna leafe \u00e6t Weogornaceastre him sealde \u00fe\u00e6t lond on ece erfe & \u00fea bec & \u00fe\u00e6t\nOnd ic Eadno\u00f0 eac beode minum erfeweardum on Godes \u00e6lmihtiges naman \u00fe\u00e6t heo n\u00e6fre \u00feis feoh\nGod \u00e6lmihtig \u00fea gehealde for b\u00e6m lifum \u00fee unne \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feeos ger\u00e6dnis stondon mote in ecnesse.\n& \u00feis syndon \u00feara manna naman \u00fee \u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6re rednisse w\u00e6ron & \u00e6t gewitnysse \u00fee her beneo\u00f0an awritene\nIc W\u00e6rfer\u00f0 bisceop mid minre a